 Worlds, but his 6-5 decision victory over Mustafin in round two was considered a big upset. His final match was just as close, a 5-4 victory over Frgić which brought the Finn the gold medal. He would later win the 1977 World Championships, with the same podium as in Montréal, with Mustafin second and Frgić third. Ukkola also won the 1977 European Championships, again with Mustafin in second place."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Round Eliminated"] [:th {} "Bad Points"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "71"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/58004"} "Pertti Ukkola"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/FIN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/FIN.png"}] "FIN"]] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "359"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/60851"} "Ivica Frgić"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/YUG"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/YUG.png"}] "YUG"]] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {:class "bib"} "328"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/60508"} "Farkhat Mustafin"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/URS"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/URS.png"}] "URS"]] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Bronze"} "Bronze"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "4"] [:td {:class "bib"} "186"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/59096"} "Yoshima Suga"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/JPN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align